**Definition 6.3 (basic extraction without callable data).** From decoded
raw $W$, or from the corresponding basic family records of an M-body, the
following finite procedure constructs consumed input and the stopping
ordinal. It reads no family-5 payload, package $I_k$, completed-cycle $M$
or saved Image.

Read the genuine seed syntax through its acquired interval and boot/origin
binding. Apply ARC Definition 6.1's slot-counted syntax conversion and pad
to the original $2H_0-1$ tokens; this yields the original single private
packet, rather than the current source. Fixed public/prior/controller
words and $E(L),\Delta(G_\circ),E(G_\circ)$ are the public apparatus code
parameters, consumed only at their real distinct original sites. Count
actual selected meter receipt cells, excluding its L/R boundaries, to
obtain $1^n$. Its marks remain data; no moving live meter end is scanned.

Recover the consumed 70 prefix as its written binary material after the
sentinel, skipping literal block Fs. A blank after EX is not a bit. The
outer body is IN(6), EX, WR(6), MR; history length additionally has its
distinct latch-5 test; history payload is RD(length,5), IN(6), EX, WR(6),
MR(70), MR(length). At an occupied IN-to-WR cut append its latch-6 bit
once; at/after WR it is already in backing and pending is empty.

Port 13 uses its **preallocated** CAP payload grammar. Header and unary
length use their actual IN/EX/WR/test/move rows. Allocation and zeroing
before payload input supply no payload bits. During its payload loop let
$b$ be the actual payload base and $p$ its marked position; compute their
difference by unary cancellation of actual positional words.

| Actual substage | Written payload extent | Extra pending bit |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Before IN, including after bound RD | $p-b$ | None |
| After IN, before WR | $p-b$ | Actual latch 5 |
| After WR, before payload MR | $p-b+1$ | None |
| After payload MR, before length MR/next RD | $p-b$ | None |
| Setup before first IN | Zero | None |
| After terminal length RD(0) | Full declared length | None |

Use actual PC and role permutation to select the row case. During incomplete
Base/length/descriptor work use its retained raw scratch/head frontier,
not a nonexistent completed descriptor. After completion the literal
sep/status boundaries and actual descriptors fix the three blocks even
if later helpers moved the head. Include an occupied header/length bit
